But 
\[(2b+3h)+ 3h+ (2b+6h) + (12-a-h) = (2b+3h) + (2b+6h) + (a+4h) + (12-a) = 20h + 12.\]Not coincidentally, this is the perimeter of $WXYZ$, being the sum of the lengths of the legs and bases of the right triangles $\triangle WAZ$, $\triangle BZX$, and $\triangle CAB$, so $h=\frac{P-k}{20}$, where $P$ is the perimeter of $WXYZ$ and $k$ is the sum of the bases $WX$ and $ZY$.

